# What NOT to ship inside the published .tgz (npm pack). These stay in the repository —
# this only trims the package a consumer downloads and installs.
#
# The release tarball was 72 MB for ~1.5 MB of actual package: 58 MB of reference PDFs and
# 13 MB of README animations, neither of which any project needs at runtime or in the
# editor. Both remain on GitHub, which is where they are read.

# Reference material: Lengyel's papers and the original C++ tables they were translated
# from. Cited in the README; not something to redistribute in every install.
Sources/
Sources.meta

# README artwork (cover image and the demo GIFs). Consequence: images in the README do not
# resolve from an installed copy of the package. That is fine — package.json's
# documentationUrl points at GitHub, which is where the README is actually read.
.github/

# Local tooling and repository plumbing.
.claude/
.gitattributes
